-- ---- s 262: the application for permission (or leave) --------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3406 | 262	Application for permission to continue claim as a derivative claim

-- src:3407 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:3408 | (a) a company has brought a claim, and
-- src:3409 | (b) the cause of action on which the claim is based could be pursued as a derivative claim under this Chapter.
-- src:3410 | (2) A member of the company may apply to the court for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) to continue the claim as a derivative claim on the ground that—
-- src:3411 | (a) the manner in which the company commenced or continued the claim amounts to an abuse of the process of the court,
-- src:3412 | (b) the company has failed to prosecute the claim diligently, and
-- src:3413 | (c) it is appropriate for the member to continue the claim as a derivative claim.
@ref s 262(1)-(2) Application for permission to continue claim as a derivative claim (src:3406-3413)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=the day the company has brought a claim that could be pursued as a derivative claim; counting=silent (s 262(2) says "may apply" and gives no time, so no clock is encoded and the power stays open until the trace shows it used)
-- FORK: s 262(2) "on the ground that (a) ..., (b) ..., and (c)" | all three grounds are needed, as the existing function reads the list joined by "and" | (a) or (b), together with (c)
GIVEN `a company has brought a claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cause of action on which the claim is based could be pursued as a derivative claim under this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manner in which the company commenced or continued the claim amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has failed to prosecute the claim diligently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate for the member to continue the claim as a derivative claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 260-264 party` `ss 260-264 act`
`s 262(2) the member's power to apply for permission to continue the company's claim as a derivative claim` MEANS
    IF (`s 262(2) the member may apply to the court for permission to continue the claim as a derivative claim`
            (`s 262(1) this section applies` `a company has brought a claim` `the cause of action on which the claim is based could be pursued as a derivative claim under this Chapter`)
            `the manner in which the company commenced or continued the claim amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` `the company has failed to prosecute the claim diligently` `it is appropriate for the member to continue the claim as a derivative claim`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `ss 260-264 the member who applies to continue the company's claim`
         MAY `s 262(2) the member applies to the court for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) to continue the claim as a derivative claim`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

