@ref s 262(4) Directions as to the evidence, and adjournment (src:3417-3419)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=the day the court decides not to dismiss the application; counting=silent (s 262(4)(a) says "may give directions" and gives no time, so no clock is encoded)
-- FORK: s 262(4)(a) "directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company" | only the court's power to give the direction is encoded: the text lays no duty on the company and no time for its evidence, which the court's own directions set | the company's duty to provide the evidence is a rule of this section
GIVEN `the application and the evidence disclose no prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 260-264 party` `ss 260-264 act`
`s 262(4)(a) the court's power to give directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company` MEANS
    IF (`s 262(4) the court may give directions as to the evidence and may adjourn the proceedings` (`s 262(3) the court must dismiss the application` `the application and the evidence disclose no prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `ss 260-264 the court`
         MAY `s 262(4)(a) the court gives directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=the day the court decides not to dismiss the application; counting=silent (s 262(4)(b) says "may adjourn the proceedings" and gives no time, so no clock is encoded)
-- FORK: s 262(4) (a) and (b) | two separate powers, each its own rule, so that using one does not finish the other | one rule offering both
GIVEN `the application and the evidence disclose no prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 260-264 party` `ss 260-264 act`
`s 262(4)(b) the court's power to adjourn the proceedings to enable the evidence to be obtained` MEANS
    IF (`s 262(4) the court may give directions as to the evidence and may adjourn the proceedings` (`s 262(3) the court must dismiss the application` `the application and the evidence disclose no prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `ss 260-264 the court`
         MAY `s 262(4)(b) the court adjourns the proceedings to enable the evidence to be obtained`
