-- ---- s 264: the application for permission (or leave) --------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3447 | 264	Application for permission to continue derivative claim brought by another member

-- src:3448 | (1) This section applies where a member of a company (“the claimant”)—
-- src:3449 | (a) has brought a derivative claim,
-- src:3450 | (b) has continued as a derivative claim a claim brought by the company, or
-- src:3451 | (c) has continued a derivative claim under this section.
-- src:3452 | (2) Another member of the company (“the applicant”) may apply to the court for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) to continue the claim on the ground that—
-- src:3453 | (a) the manner in which the proceedings have been commenced or continued by the claimant amounts to an abuse of the process of the court,
-- src:3454 | (b) the claimant has failed to prosecute the claim diligently, and
-- src:3455 | (c) it is appropriate for the applicant to continue the claim as a derivative claim.
@ref s 264(1)-(2) Application for permission to continue derivative claim brought by another member (src:3447-3455)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=the day the claimant has brought or continued the derivative claim; counting=silent (s 264(2) says "may apply" and gives no time, so no clock is encoded and the power stays open until the trace shows it used)
-- FORK: s 264(2) "on the ground that (a) ..., (b) ..., and (c)" | all three grounds are needed, as the existing function reads the list joined by "and" | (a) or (b), together with (c)
GIVEN `a member of the company (“the claimant”) has brought a derivative claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has continued as a derivative claim a claim brought by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has continued a derivative claim under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manner in which the proceedings have been commenced or continued by the claimant amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has failed to prosecute the claim diligently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate for the applicant to continue the claim as a derivative claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 260-264 party` `ss 260-264 act`
`s 264(2) another member's power to apply for permission to continue the claim` MEANS
    IF (`s 264(2) another member may apply to the court for permission to continue the claim`
            (`s 264(1) this section applies` `a member of the company (“the claimant”) has brought a derivative claim` `the claimant has continued as a derivative claim a claim brought by the company` `the claimant has continued a derivative claim under this section`)
            `the manner in which the proceedings have been commenced or continued by the claimant amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` `the claimant has failed to prosecute the claim diligently` `it is appropriate for the applicant to continue the claim as a derivative claim`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `ss 260-264 another member of the company`
         MAY `s 264(2) another member applies to the court for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) to continue the claim`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ---- s 264(3): the court dismisses an application that discloses no prima facie case, and may make a consequential order ------

-- src:3456 | (3) If it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave), the court—
-- src:3457 | (a) must dismiss the application, and
-- src:3458 | (b) may make any consequential order it considers appropriate.
@ref s 264(3) Dismissal where no prima facie case, and any consequential order (src:3456-3458)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=the day it appears to the court that the application and the evidence disclose no prima facie case; counting=silent (s 264(3) says "must dismiss" and gives no time, so no clock is encoded and the duty stays owed until the trace shows it done)
-- FORK: s 264(3) "it appears to the court" | the court's view is an input to the rule, and the duty to dismiss arises when the input is true | the duty arises only once the court has stated its view in a decision
GIVEN `the application and the evidence disclose no prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 260-264 party` `ss 260-264 act`
`s 264(3)(a) the court's step of dismissing an application that discloses no prima facie case` MEANS
    IF (`s 264(3) the court must dismiss the application` `the application and the evidence disclose no prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `ss 260-264 the court`
         MUST `s 264(3)(a) the court dismisses the application`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=the day the court dismisses the application; counting=silent (s 264(3)(b) says "may make any consequential order it considers appropriate" and gives no time, so no clock is encoded and the power stays open until the trace shows it used)
-- FORK: s 264(3)(b) "may make any consequential order" | a separate power of the court, open only where the court must dismiss, and not a condition of the dismissal being complete | the consequential order is the next step of the dismissal, so a dismissal with no order is unfinished
GIVEN `the application and the evidence disclose no prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 260-264 party` `ss 260-264 act`
`s 264(3)(b) the court's power to make a consequential order after a dismissal` MEANS
    IF (`s 264(3)(b) the court may make any consequential order it considers appropriate` (`s 264(3) the court must dismiss the application` `the application and the evidence disclose no prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `ss 260-264 the court`
         MAY `s 264(3)(b) the court makes a consequential order`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

